WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:13.940
Secure LLM integration means safely connecting Python applications to language models while controlling the data, credentials, prompts, retrieval sources, tools, outputs, and monitoring around that connection.

2
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:27.000
The model may be reached through a hosted API, local runtime, internal gateway, SDK, or service wrapper, but the security responsibility does not end at the call boundary.

3
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:34.780
The integration must decide what is sent, who is allowed to request it, what authority the model has, and what happens with the response.

4
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:47.300
LLM integrations appear in chat assistants, document summarizers, retrieval systems, coding helpers, customer support tools, workflow assistants, data analysis tools, and internal automation.

5
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:53.320
These systems may look conversational, but they often sit near sensitive data and business processes.

6
00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.460
A summarizer may read confidential documents.

7
00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.800
A coding helper may see source code.

8
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.700
A workflow assistant may draft tickets, query systems, or propose changes.

9
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:08.200
Security depends on the surrounding application, not only on the model's behavior.

10
00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:17.840
It helps to separate the model, the Python application, the API client, the prompt, the context, the retrieval layer, tools, logs, and user interface.

11
00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:21.700
The model generates text or structured output from context.

12
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:25.480
The application assembles that context and enforces policy.

13
00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:31.420
The API client handles credentials, requests, retries, and provider boundaries.

14
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.280
Retrieval finds supporting data.

15
00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.220
Tools perform capabilities.

16
00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:36.920
Logs preserve traces.

17
00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.500
The interface shapes user decisions.

18
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.760
Each layer has different controls.

19
00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.440
Ordinary Python security still applies.

20
00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:58.140
Authentication, authorization, secret handling, TLS validation, dependency review, input validation, output handling, safe errors, logging, monitoring, and incident response remain necessary.

21
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:08.800
LLM-specific risks appear when natural-language input can influence data access, decisions, generated output, tool calls, or downstream actions.

22
00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:16.100
A secure integration keeps the model useful while preventing it from becoming an unsupervised authority over sensitive systems.
